CREATED-BY: N1MM Logger+ 1.0.9883.0
SOAPBOX: I was able to use the P45 PFX once again this year, celebrating 50 years Aruba Anthem & Flag and 40 years Status Aparte, so had lots of fun again!
SOAPBOX: Had a feeling the band was not as good as last year and on top of that made a rookie mistake on Friday evening, due to my rotor control set-up, of beaming in the wrong direction for the US, loosing most probably a good run in the US that evening....
SOAPBOX: Europe was great on Saturday with great signals and a good consistent pile-up, Sunday was not as good.
SOAPBOX: Issue remains being spotted wrongly, P44A, P54A and CP45A where just a few this time around. When a few dupes after each other start to show up, you know some one spotted you wrong, especially when the other side insist they did not work you yet....
SOAPBOX: Clearly, AI does not understand that either, so it is of no use to try to explain that to AI when being called for the third time by that station.
SOAPBOX: All by all did a little better then last year and also in 2016 when I used the P45 PFX for the first time.
SOAPBOX: TNX to all that gave me a call and had the patience bearing with me sometimes to pull out their call and number exchange, especially some JA's that were just above my noise level!
SOAPBOX: Great to hear a couple more locals on the air, so congrats also go to P43K, P43L and P49Y for their great efforts!
SOAPBOX: Using: Yaesu FTDX5000, Heil HC5, Acom 2000A, single home brewed 5 El. Yagi at 50' and N1MM logging
SOAPBOX: 73's de P43A, Jean-Pierre
